I reach the clinic and go inside.
The clinic is small, but it is very crowded there.
I sit on an empty chair in the waiting room.
I sit with my eyes closed.
There are two more patients in the clinic.
An elderly man is sitting next to me.
He is coughing a lot.
A young mother is sitting opposite.
She has her small child with her.
That child is being very restless.
The mother is lovingly calming him down.
Many people here are sick.
I wait patiently for my name.
After a short while, the receptionist calls my name.
She says, "Maya Madam, it is your turn now."
"You should go inside now."
I stand up slowly.
Finally my name is called.
I go towards the cabin to see the doctor.
